1
00:03:46,956 --> 00:03:52,956
You'll wish it was only make-believe.

2
00:07:33,913 --> 00:07:39,913
Child's Play is a horror film directed by Tom Holland.

3
00:11:20,869 --> 00:11:26,869
After being shot in a toy store, a serial killer
transfers his soul into a Good Guy doll.

4
00:15:07,826 --> 00:15:13,826
A mother then gifts it to her 6-year old son Andy,
which unleashes terror upon the city.

5
00:18:54,782 --> 00:19:00,782
Andy Barclay, played by Alex Vincent.

6
00:22:41,739 --> 00:22:47,739
Chucky (voice) / Charles Lee Ray, played by Brad Dourif.

7
00:26:28,695 --> 00:26:34,695
Karen Barclay, played by Catherine Hicks.

8
00:30:15,652 --> 00:30:21,652
Mike Norris, played by Chris Sarandon.

9
00:34:02,608 --> 00:34:08,608
Maggie Peterson, played by Dinah Manoff.

10
00:37:49,565 --> 00:37:55,565
Jack Santos, played by Tommy Swerdlow.

11
00:41:36,521 --> 00:41:42,521
Child's Play is a 1988 American supernatural slasher film directed by Tom Holland, from a
screenplay he co-wrote with Don Mancini and John Lafia based on a story by Mancini.

12
00:45:23,478 --> 00:45:29,478
The film stars Catherine Hicks and Chris Sarandon with
Brad Dourif as the voice of Chucky.

13
00:49:10,434 --> 00:49:16,434
Its plot follows a widowed mother who gives a new doll to her son,
unaware that it is possessed by the soul of a serial killer.

14
00:52:57,391 --> 00:53:03,391
Child's Play was released in the United States on
November 9, 1988, by MGM/UA Communications Co.

15
00:56:44,347 --> 00:56:50,347
through its United Artists label.

16
01:00:31,304 --> 01:00:37,304
It received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed more than
$44 million against a production budget of $9 million.

17
01:04:18,260 --> 01:04:24,260
Along with the film gaining a cult following, the box office success also spawned a media franchise that includes a
series of six sequels, a television series, merchandise, novels, comic books, a video game, and a reboot.

18
01:08:05,217 --> 01:08:11,217
The original Child's Play film was distributed by United Artists, although the
rights to the series were sold to Universal Pictures in 1990.

19
01:11:52,173 --> 01:11:58,173
MGM (via United Artists) retained the rights to the original film and Orion Pictures
(through United Artists Releasing) also distributed the reboot in 2019.

20
01:15:39,130 --> 01:15:45,130
A sequel, Child's Play 2, was released in 1990.

21
01:19:26,086 --> 01:19:32,086
The film explores themes of chicago, illinois, birthday, gun, voodoo, stalker.

22
01:23:13,043 --> 01:23:19,043
The tone is dark.
